ite resistant to certain  conditions it is resistant to cold  okay it's like cold conditions and it  can still survive and persist but  interestingly not hot  so it's good if the environment the  temperature is becoming  unfavorably cool but not very helpful if  the temperature is increasing  and getting hot it's also the acnes are  resistant  to desiccation  remember that desiccation is a fancy  word  for drying  so resistant to when things get very  very dry and there's not much water  available so when it's becoming  dehydrated  um another characteristic of acne is  that they are enlarged at least compared  to vegetative cells okay so over here in  green i've drawn the vegetative  cyanobacteria  you can see that they are a lot smaller  than this great big acne so the acne is  quite large compared to  like a normal kind of metabolically  active vegetated cyanobacterium  now when do the acnes develop well a  vegetative cell  can  develop into an acne when conditions  become unfavorable  so this might be triggered  by insufficient light  remember that  cyanobacteria  are photosynthetic  so so if there's insufficient light  to meet their energy requirements  these vegetative cells might be  triggered to develop into acne  insufficient nutrients  will  also  cause  this development into acne or  unfavorable  temperatures  [Music]  or unfavorable salinity basically if the  salt concentration is getting outside of  its preferred range  these are all things that basically are  unfavorable conditions that might  trigger  a vegetative cell  to turn into an acne  now when conditions become more  favorable the acne can germinate that  simply means returning to the vegetative  state  so to germinate would have the acne  developing back into a vegetative  cell  now i want you to make sure you realize  that acnes are not entirely dormant okay  now endospores basically are they're  basically dormant structures and a  holding pattern just waiting for  conditions to become more fa